{"name":"Bored Accent Green","hex":"#dedd98","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bored","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of bore"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Suffering from boredom; mildly annoyed and restless through having nothing to do.","Perforated by a hole or holes."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bored"},{"term":"accent","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A higher-pitched or stronger (louder or longer) articulation of a particular syllable of a word or phrase in order to distinguish it from the others or to emphasize it.","Emphasis or importance in general."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To express the accent of vocally; to utter with accent.","To mark emphatically; to emphasize; to accentuate; to make prominent."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/accent"},{"term":"green","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of grass and leaves; a primary additive color midway between yellow and blue which is evoked by light between roughly 495–570 nm.","A member of a green party; an environmentalist."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a green hue.","Sickly, unwell."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/green"}],"entries":[{"title":"Boredom","blocks":[{"text":"In conventional usage, boredom, ennui, or tedium is an emotion characterized by uninterest in one's surrounding, often caused by a lack of distractions or occupations. However, boredom is not well defined. It is distinct from depression and apathy. Boredom may damage mental health, but it also seems to have improved creativity in humans."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Souvenir_Seller_-_Moscow_-_Russia_cropped.JPG/330px-Souvenir_Seller_-_Moscow_-_Russia_cropped.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boredom"},{"title":"Green","blocks":[{"text":"Green is the color between cyan and yellow on the visible spectrum. It has 295–350 different shades. It is evoked by light which has a dominant wavelength of roughly 495–570 nm. In subtractive color systems, used in painting and color printing, it is created by a combination of yellow and cyan; in the RGB color model, used on television and computer screens, it is one of the additive primary colors, along with red and blue, which are mixed in different combinations to create all other colors. By far the largest contributor to green in nature is chlorophyll, the chemical by which plants photosynthesize and convert sunlight into chemical energy. Many creatures have adapted to their green environments by taking on a green hue themselves as camouflage. Several minerals have a green color, including the emerald, which is colored green by its chromium content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg/330px-Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/La_Touche_Lennui_1893.jpg/500px-La_Touche_Lennui_1893.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/La_Touche_Lennui_1893.jpg/500px-La_Touche_Lennui_1893.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Boredom by Gaston de La Touche, 1893","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALa_Touche_Lennui_1893.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Bored_girl.jpg/500px-Bored_girl.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Bored_girl.jpg/1280px-Bored_girl.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campai